WEBVTT

00:00:19.193 --> 00:00:20.933
&lt;i&gt;RUTHERFORD:
Ooh! I'm pooped.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:21.064 --> 00:00:23.023
Working on ocean planets
really takes it out of you.

00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:25.112
- [grunting]
- I love cataloging algae
as much as anyone,

00:00:25.286 --> 00:00:27.244
but keep it to
a thousand mutations or less.

00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:29.638
Yeah, I think I'm not gonna
come back to Piskes Nine

00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:31.292
until at least tenth contact.

00:00:31.379 --> 00:00:33.033
What are you talking about?
That was fun.

00:00:33.163 --> 00:00:36.123
Hmm. Well, you don't
have a fever.

00:00:36.297 --> 00:00:38.125
Oh, stop, stop.
Sure, it was a lot of work

00:00:38.255 --> 00:00:40.127
that old Mariner
would have definitely hated

00:00:40.257 --> 00:00:41.780
but, hey, that algae
glowed in the dark.

00:00:41.911 --> 00:00:43.608
Oh!
I love bioluminescence too.

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:46.133
Mariner! I never took you
for a seaweed girl.

00:00:46.263 --> 00:00:47.960
Mm, not when you
phrase it like that, I'm not.

00:00:48.091 --> 00:00:50.311
I-I don't know, I guess I'm
just starting to enjoy missions

00:00:50.398 --> 00:00:52.226
without trying to fight
the system or whatever.

00:00:52.356 --> 00:00:54.228
Doing granular science
is what Starfleet's all about

00:00:54.358 --> 00:00:56.578
and wow, I sound like
a real Boimler right now.

00:00:56.752 --> 00:00:58.580
Yeah. Uh, cool as hell.
[chuckles]

00:00:58.754 --> 00:01:00.060
[grunts] Oh! Aah!

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.887
You've really come
a long way, Mariner.

00:01:02.018 --> 00:01:03.367
I find it inspiring.

00:01:03.498 --> 00:01:06.979
- [alarm blaring]
- Ooh, I like red alerts, too.

00:01:07.154 --> 00:01:09.286
Come on, danger time.

00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:10.592
Captain, we dropped out of warp

00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:12.507
due to a navigational
malfunction.

00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:13.856
Captain to Cetacean Ops.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:15.988
Lieutenant, what's your status?

00:01:21.559 --> 00:01:23.213
&lt;i&gt;[screaming]&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:23.344 --> 00:01:26.434
Computer, shut down
nav processing.

00:01:26.564 --> 00:01:28.131
We are supposed to be
at a captains' conference

00:01:28.218 --> 00:01:30.264
on Casperia Prime
in 24 hours.

00:01:30.394 --> 00:01:33.049
I'm hosting their first annual
scatting battle.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.137
Well, we aren't
gonna be anywhere

00:01:34.268 --> 00:01:35.617
unless we get the nav repaired.

00:01:35.791 --> 00:01:38.315
Mr. Boimler, are there
any starbases within impulse?

00:01:38.446 --> 00:01:40.578
BOIMLER:
Yes, but you're not
gonna like it.

00:01:40.709 --> 00:01:42.580
The only station
within reach is

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.016
Starbase 80.

00:01:44.147 --> 00:01:45.844
- [crew gasps]
- MALE: Damn. Starbase 80?!

00:01:45.975 --> 00:01:48.412
- That's the worst starbase
in the quadrant!
- [grunts]

00:01:48.499 --> 00:01:50.327
No, no, I am not
going back to the hellhole.

00:01:50.458 --> 00:01:53.200
I'm a positive person now.
I love algae.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:54.418
There's nowhere else?

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:55.463
I mean, at full impulse

00:01:55.637 --> 00:01:56.551
we could get to Deep Space Six

00:01:56.681 --> 00:01:58.205
in 400 years.

00:01:58.335 --> 00:01:59.858
That. Let's do that.
Mom, please. Right?

00:01:59.989 --> 00:02:01.643
We-we can't go to Starbase 80.

00:02:01.773 --> 00:02:02.818
Let's just, you know,
put out a distress call

00:02:02.948 --> 00:02:04.559
and drift until we get rescued.

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:07.039
As much as I would love to
never set foot on that station,

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.693
we need a navigation processor.

00:02:08.867 --> 00:02:10.042
It's our only option.

00:02:10.217 --> 00:02:13.220
Mr. Boimler, Starbase 80,
full impulse.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:16.310
No...!

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.922
Are you gonna do that
the whole way there?

00:02:20.052 --> 00:02:22.446
&lt;i&gt;[Mariner continuing]&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:26.233
♪ ♪

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:48.255
♪ ♪

00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:19.242
♪

00:03:39.523 --> 00:03:41.264
♪ ♪

00:03:43.875 --> 00:03:45.703
Absolutely not.
You can't make me go back.

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:47.488
Put me in the brig.
Shoot me into space.

00:03:47.618 --> 00:03:50.099
I don't want to be
on SB80 any more than you do.

00:03:50.273 --> 00:03:51.579
When we crossed dimensions,

00:03:51.709 --> 00:03:53.668
the other me
ran this pile of junk.

00:03:53.798 --> 00:03:56.061
- Now, you've been here.
- Because you banished me!

00:03:56.192 --> 00:03:58.107
And I apologize for that.

00:03:58.281 --> 00:04:00.544
Is it really
infested with fleas?

00:04:00.675 --> 00:04:02.764
Denobulan lice.
And they itch like [bleep].

00:04:02.851 --> 00:04:05.375
This place is cursed.
I've already been here too long.

00:04:05.462 --> 00:04:08.030
We'll be in and out
as fast as possible.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.337
I'm sure it won't be that bad.

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.034
Hey, Captain,
Starbase 80's transporters

00:04:12.121 --> 00:04:13.557
aren't safe for organic use.

00:04:13.731 --> 00:04:15.777
They want us to rub down
with some kind of gel.

00:04:15.951 --> 00:04:18.301
Ha! See? The curse begins.

00:04:23.915 --> 00:04:26.527
Check me out.
I'm a total T'Pol over here.

00:04:26.614 --> 00:04:27.484
Mare-Bear, get my back.

00:04:27.571 --> 00:04:29.051
Not if my life depended on it.

00:04:29.225 --> 00:04:30.531
Also, why do we
have to decontaminate?

00:04:30.661 --> 00:04:32.576
They're the ones
who are cursed, not us.

00:04:32.707 --> 00:04:34.796
Come on, you can't really
believe in curses.

00:04:34.926 --> 00:04:36.493
I didn't used to,
but I've seen it.

00:04:36.624 --> 00:04:38.843
A regular smart person
spends too much time here

00:04:39.017 --> 00:04:40.845
and somehow,
through mysterious forces,

00:04:41.019 --> 00:04:42.282
thy turn into a total buffoon.

00:04:42.369 --> 00:04:44.240
That's a little unscientific.

00:04:44.371 --> 00:04:46.634
- Can science explain Q?
- Probably.

00:04:46.764 --> 00:04:48.244
You gonna use all your gel?

00:04:48.418 --> 00:04:49.811
Ooh, hey, man, I wouldn't
use too much of that stuff.

00:04:49.941 --> 00:04:51.160
I think there's a reason
they got rid of it.

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:53.815
I like to lay it on thick.

00:04:53.989 --> 00:04:56.383
Oh, yeah, that's the stuff.

00:05:00.604 --> 00:05:03.303
Mariner, the ground isn't gonna
fall out from under you.

00:05:03.477 --> 00:05:04.869
Last time I was here,
I fell into an open ditch.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.828
Now, I know
what you're thinking.

00:05:06.958 --> 00:05:08.351
You're like, "How can there
be an open ditch on a starbase?"

00:05:08.482 --> 00:05:09.961
Well, anything's possible
in hell.

00:05:10.092 --> 00:05:12.050
- Hiya, &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; crew!
- Aah!

00:05:12.224 --> 00:05:14.575
[laughs]
Welcome to Starbase 80.

00:05:14.662 --> 00:05:16.968
Kassia Nox, diplomatic liaison.

00:05:17.099 --> 00:05:19.884
We're so relieved Starfleet
finally sent someone

00:05:20.058 --> 00:05:21.408
to repair our flux spectrometer.

00:05:21.582 --> 00:05:23.366
I'm afraid there's been
a misunderstanding.

00:05:23.497 --> 00:05:25.150
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; was forced here

00:05:25.281 --> 00:05:26.630
due to a navigational
malfunction.

00:05:26.761 --> 00:05:28.806
We need a new processor,
if you have one.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.504
Oh, I see.

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:32.506
Well, I'm sure we have
a nav processor or two

00:05:32.636 --> 00:05:34.769
in storage, as long as you
don't mind an older model.

00:05:34.899 --> 00:05:37.511
[all exclaim]

00:05:37.641 --> 00:05:40.470
Well, the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; isn't exactly
cutting edge either.

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.472
So, older--
it-it should be fine.

00:05:42.559 --> 00:05:44.344
I'm sure my chief engineer
can help you.

00:05:44.474 --> 00:05:45.867
He's down on level 15.

00:05:45.997 --> 00:05:47.912
Mariner, why don't you
go see if you can help

00:05:48.086 --> 00:05:49.218
with any station repairs

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.088
while we
go and get the processor.

00:05:50.219 --> 00:05:51.612
Ooh, alternate idea.

00:05:51.699 --> 00:05:53.004
I would love to go back
to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:53.178 --> 00:05:53.962
and not help with anything.

00:05:54.049 --> 00:05:56.878
That's an order.

00:05:57.008 --> 00:05:58.880
Looks like you're with me.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.882
Mom, come on. Please, please,
look, give me-give me

00:06:01.056 --> 00:06:01.839
holodeck waste removal duty.

00:06:02.013 --> 00:06:03.493
Anything that takes me

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.538
back to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;
Please.

00:06:04.668 --> 00:06:06.801
Ah, man, these systems
are all old and weird.

00:06:06.888 --> 00:06:09.194
I was dreaming about
working on something new.

00:06:09.281 --> 00:06:11.545
Have you dreamed
of being cursed?

00:06:19.117 --> 00:06:20.336
So, what crime did you commit

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:22.033
to get you banished
to Curse Town?

00:06:22.164 --> 00:06:23.731
None.
I volunteered.

00:06:23.861 --> 00:06:25.559
That's weird. You sure
that's how it went down?

00:06:25.689 --> 00:06:27.952
SB80 might not be
the most glamorous starbase

00:06:28.126 --> 00:06:30.999
in the Federation,
but it grows on you.

00:06:31.086 --> 00:06:33.088
Like a fungus.

00:06:33.175 --> 00:06:35.873
Welcome to Engineering.
Watch your step.

00:06:37.745 --> 00:06:39.660
- Uh...
- [all exclaim]

00:06:41.749 --> 00:06:43.620
RUTHERFORD:
Whoa, we're on the ceiling.

00:06:43.751 --> 00:06:45.709
Oh, yeah, well,
we're having a little trouble

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.363
with the gravity plating.
[chuckles]

00:06:47.537 --> 00:06:50.671
Oh! The fusion reactor
is so cute.

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:53.238
Oh, my gosh.
And do you use wall comms?

00:06:53.369 --> 00:06:54.718
- [boatswain's whistle blows]
- The base hasn't experienced

00:06:54.849 --> 00:06:56.851
many upgrades since the 2260s.

00:06:56.938 --> 00:06:59.984
That's why it's so retro cool!

00:07:00.158 --> 00:07:01.464
See, Mariner?
No curse here.

00:07:01.551 --> 00:07:03.292
Just a minimalist
reactor room

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.772
with a... corn dog vendor?

00:07:04.902 --> 00:07:06.730
- KASSIA: That's Chad.
- Oh.

00:07:06.817 --> 00:07:08.863
You have to try his corn dogs--
they're incredible.

00:07:08.993 --> 00:07:10.168
Mmm, mmm, mmm!

00:07:10.299 --> 00:07:11.082
They have food vendors
all over the base

00:07:11.213 --> 00:07:12.954
instead of replicators.

00:07:13.084 --> 00:07:14.738
We've actually found that
the absence of replicators

00:07:14.869 --> 00:07:17.698
has livened the station's
culinary scene.

00:07:17.828 --> 00:07:20.135
Looks like the gravity
stabilizer's working,

00:07:20.222 --> 00:07:22.354
just, you know,
in the wrong direction.

00:07:22.529 --> 00:07:23.878
Rutherford to Commander Billups.

00:07:24.008 --> 00:07:25.488
&lt;i&gt;[low moaning]&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:25.619 --> 00:07:27.142
SB80's got some problems
with their grav plating.

00:07:27.316 --> 00:07:29.361
Can you help out?
Aah! Static.

00:07:29.536 --> 00:07:31.407
Yep, this place is charged up.

00:07:31.538 --> 00:07:32.669
Don't walk around in your socks.

00:07:32.756 --> 00:07:34.541
What was up with that
incoherent moaning?

00:07:34.671 --> 00:07:36.325
Guess the breakfast burrito
didn't sit well.

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:37.979
Looks like I'm on my own.

00:07:38.109 --> 00:07:39.807
Well, we still have
the old schematics in storage

00:07:39.937 --> 00:07:42.026
- that came with the station.
- Awesome!

00:07:42.157 --> 00:07:44.551
Wait, I thought Billups
only ate hot cereals.

00:07:44.638 --> 00:07:46.770
Well, he's been working on
his pickiness. I'm proud of him.

00:07:46.944 --> 00:07:50.208
Proud or concerned for
out of character curse behavior?

00:07:50.339 --> 00:07:53.211
It was a burrito, and Billups
isn't even on SB80.

00:07:53.385 --> 00:07:54.517
He's back on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:54.604 --> 00:07:57.128
That's true. All right.
Maybe we're okay.

00:08:00.262 --> 00:08:01.872
♪ ♪

00:08:02.003 --> 00:08:03.787
[growling]

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:07.487
[thud]

00:08:07.574 --> 00:08:10.359
[sniffs]
Oof! My, this place

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:11.839
does have a signature stink.

00:08:11.969 --> 00:08:13.928
Mmm!
All I smell is gel.

00:08:14.015 --> 00:08:15.146
- [shouting in distance]
- Do you hear that?

00:08:15.277 --> 00:08:17.018
- [alarm blaring]
- [gasps]

00:08:17.148 --> 00:08:18.585
Is that man dead?

00:08:20.282 --> 00:08:21.718
- Aah!
- [gasps]

00:08:21.849 --> 00:08:22.676
Oh.

00:08:22.806 --> 00:08:24.025
Howdy.

00:08:24.155 --> 00:08:25.766
Y'all must be from the &lt;i&gt;'Ritos,&lt;/i&gt;
aren't you?

00:08:25.853 --> 00:08:27.202
Sorry, dozed off there.

00:08:27.376 --> 00:08:29.247
With all these alarms going off?

00:08:29.378 --> 00:08:32.642
Oh, hell, I don't have the tools
to reroute their microcircuits.

00:08:32.773 --> 00:08:34.862
Don't worry,
you'll get used to it.

00:08:34.992 --> 00:08:36.037
[sighs]

00:08:40.389 --> 00:08:42.826
[laughs]
Hot damn! Y'all got

00:08:42.957 --> 00:08:44.959
them really good
modern tricorders.

00:08:45.046 --> 00:08:47.701
Happy to help. We're looking
for the chief engineer.

00:08:47.831 --> 00:08:49.659
He has a navigation
processor for us.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:51.400
Oh, hell, that's Jakobowski.

00:08:51.574 --> 00:08:53.358
Great guy.
Hell of a throwing arm.

00:08:53.445 --> 00:08:55.273
Uh-huh.
And where is he?

00:08:55.404 --> 00:08:57.101
Probably in the arcade.

00:08:57.232 --> 00:08:59.103
We don't have
any fancy holodecks,

00:08:59.234 --> 00:09:01.366
so Chief spends
a lot of time there.

00:09:01.453 --> 00:09:03.543
Yeah, it's up on, uh, 33.

00:09:03.717 --> 00:09:04.761
He'll get you
that nav thingy you want.

00:09:04.848 --> 00:09:07.416
[groans] Wha...
We just came down from 33.

00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:09.374
Y'all have fun.

00:09:09.461 --> 00:09:11.072
- [snores]
- All right, Captain,

00:09:11.202 --> 00:09:12.464
let's follow this napkin.

00:09:12.595 --> 00:09:15.119
Oh, dang gel.
I got it, I got it.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:17.034
Oh, please.

00:09:17.121 --> 00:09:19.689
♪ ♪

00:09:28.132 --> 00:09:29.220
[low growling]

00:09:29.351 --> 00:09:31.353
Wow, that's a lot
of growling and glaring.

00:09:31.483 --> 00:09:33.573
Fun fact: SB80 actually has

00:09:33.703 --> 00:09:35.575
the largest population
of Acamarians

00:09:35.749 --> 00:09:37.881
outside Acamar III
due to an old negotiation hiccup

00:09:38.055 --> 00:09:40.362
that surrendered half
the starbase to their authority.

00:09:40.536 --> 00:09:42.277
Yeah, this place
is basically controlled

00:09:42.407 --> 00:09:44.148
- by a knife gang.
- [whimpers]

00:09:44.279 --> 00:09:45.628
We've sort of been hoping

00:09:45.715 --> 00:09:47.543
Starfleet might
renegotiate the treaty.

00:09:47.674 --> 00:09:50.328
But I guess it's low
on the diplomatic to-do list.

00:09:50.459 --> 00:09:51.939
[gasps]
Ruthie!

00:09:52.113 --> 00:09:53.331
No, that's cursed sauce.
Don't touch that.

00:09:53.462 --> 00:09:56.073
Wha? I eat those every day.
They're great.

00:09:56.204 --> 00:09:59.250
Uncovered and unrefrigerated?
Ugh, that's a pass.

00:09:59.381 --> 00:10:00.861
Oh!
These are cozy.

00:10:00.948 --> 00:10:02.732
How did you make them
without replicators?

00:10:02.906 --> 00:10:05.169
They're the uniforms
of long-dead men.

00:10:05.256 --> 00:10:06.736
Vintage.

00:10:08.695 --> 00:10:11.741
KASSIA:
The grav-plate manual
should be in here somewhere.

00:10:11.915 --> 00:10:13.177
It's a mess!

00:10:13.308 --> 00:10:14.701
Oh, my God, we're never
getting out of here.

00:10:14.875 --> 00:10:16.572
Okay, don't worry.
We'll divide and conquer.

00:10:16.703 --> 00:10:17.965
Rutherford, how about you
take that pile on the left?

00:10:18.052 --> 00:10:20.271
[groaning]

00:10:21.795 --> 00:10:22.839
Everything okay, buddy?

00:10:22.926 --> 00:10:24.406
- Yeah.
- BOIMLER: Whoa!

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:25.494
What are you doing? Stop that.

00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:27.017
Rutherford's cursed!
He's got the 80!

00:10:27.148 --> 00:10:30.107
There's got to be a rational,
scientific explanation...

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.284
[snarling]

00:10:35.112 --> 00:10:35.852
[roars]

00:10:35.983 --> 00:10:36.853
- [gasps]
- Ew.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.899
Okay, maybe there's a curse.

00:10:44.687 --> 00:10:45.688
[chuckles] Oh!

00:10:45.819 --> 00:10:46.907
A twist-handle control.

00:10:47.037 --> 00:10:48.517
Did you use these as an ensign?

00:10:48.648 --> 00:10:50.693
- I am not that old.
- Oh.

00:10:50.824 --> 00:10:53.435
Well, I think we turn it
to use voice command.

00:10:54.131 --> 00:10:55.567
[both exclaim]

00:10:56.264 --> 00:10:57.569
Computer, Arcade.

00:10:57.744 --> 00:10:59.006
&lt;i&gt;COMPUTER:
Maintenance labyrinth.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:59.136 --> 00:11:00.268
I said Arcade.

00:11:00.355 --> 00:11:01.922
[exclaiming]

00:11:02.052 --> 00:11:03.706
&lt;i&gt;COMPUTER:
Maintenance labyrinth confirmed.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:09.277
This is definitely
not the Arcade.

00:11:09.407 --> 00:11:10.495
&lt;i&gt;COMPUTER:
Arcade.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:10.626 --> 00:11:12.410
Get back here!
Damn it.

00:11:12.541 --> 00:11:14.151
Should I call
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; for help?

00:11:14.282 --> 00:11:17.546
No. This place got the better
of my alternate universe self.

00:11:17.677 --> 00:11:19.330
It won't do the same to me.

00:11:19.417 --> 00:11:20.680
You're still worried
about that?

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:21.985
Yes!

00:11:22.116 --> 00:11:23.334
[growling]

00:11:23.465 --> 00:11:25.032
[shouts]

00:11:25.162 --> 00:11:26.337
Look at 'em,

00:11:26.468 --> 00:11:27.643
all vacant, weird.

00:11:27.774 --> 00:11:29.819
They've all got
Starbase 80 curse.

00:11:34.911 --> 00:11:38.262
Uh, Dr. T'Ana?
- [growling, meowing nearby]

00:11:38.436 --> 00:11:40.308
- Ow.
- MARINER: [gasps] It got Dr. T.

00:11:40.438 --> 00:11:41.918
KASSIA:
Huh, that's weird.

00:11:42.049 --> 00:11:44.225
While your crew's affected,
none of us locals are.

00:11:44.399 --> 00:11:46.227
Yeah, 'cause
you're already cursed.

00:11:46.314 --> 00:11:47.924
Come on, our doctor
will get to the bottom of this.

00:11:48.055 --> 00:11:49.273
What if he's cursed, too?

00:11:49.404 --> 00:11:50.927
Well, you sort of
don't have a choice.

00:11:51.014 --> 00:11:52.494
[groans]

00:11:53.756 --> 00:11:54.626
Hello?

00:11:54.801 --> 00:11:57.847
- Lt. Jakobowski?
- [growling]

00:12:00.371 --> 00:12:02.809
- [roaring]
- [gasps]

00:12:02.939 --> 00:12:04.549
[muffled roar]

00:12:05.289 --> 00:12:06.595
FREEMAN:
Gene?

00:12:06.682 --> 00:12:08.597
Why is your head in that tube?

00:12:08.728 --> 00:12:09.511
GENE:
I'm just trying to fix

00:12:09.641 --> 00:12:11.905
an oxygen leak and I got stuck.

00:12:12.079 --> 00:12:13.950
Hold on, I've got some gel
that should help with that.

00:12:15.038 --> 00:12:17.998
- [grunting]
- [screeching]

00:12:19.173 --> 00:12:20.391
[laughs]

00:12:20.478 --> 00:12:22.306
Way too many bats around here.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.744
Gene, we need to find
your engineer.

00:12:24.918 --> 00:12:27.137
I feel like we've been just
wondering around the station

00:12:27.224 --> 00:12:28.617
fixing things.

00:12:28.748 --> 00:12:30.184
Well, since you mentioned it...

00:12:30.314 --> 00:12:31.359
What now?

00:12:31.489 --> 00:12:32.926
I don't have the know-how

00:12:33.056 --> 00:12:35.145
to get this oxygen leak sealed.
Could you...

00:12:35.276 --> 00:12:37.800
Yes.
[grunts]

00:12:43.414 --> 00:12:45.112
There. Done.

00:12:45.199 --> 00:12:48.071
Now, will you please
point us to Lt. Jakobowski?

00:12:48.158 --> 00:12:51.466
Oh, happily.
Let's get you to that arcade.

00:12:54.469 --> 00:12:56.819
[laughs]
Stairs! Boom!

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:58.429
Don't see these
in space very often.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:12:59.822
The perfect workout.

00:12:59.909 --> 00:13:01.868
Yeah, 30 stories
and you'll hit the arcade.

00:13:01.998 --> 00:13:02.825
Can't miss it.

00:13:02.956 --> 00:13:04.871
I'm not letting this place win.

00:13:05.045 --> 00:13:06.655
You're welcome.

00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:09.136
Ha, ha, my glutes.
You feel that, Cap?

00:13:09.266 --> 00:13:10.920
The power of stairs!

00:13:11.094 --> 00:13:13.096
[growling]

00:13:13.183 --> 00:13:15.403
Ugh, Tendi, Rutherford keeps
trying to lick the walls.

00:13:15.533 --> 00:13:16.970
Can you help, please?

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.494
- [growling]
- MARINER: [gasps] No!

00:13:19.624 --> 00:13:20.669
Tendi's cursed, too.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.889
Ensigns Mackler and Gorm,

00:13:23.019 --> 00:13:24.325
I need your help
at my location now.

00:13:24.455 --> 00:13:26.109
&lt;i&gt;[Mackler growling]&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:28.938
Oh, you were right, this curse
is getting to everyone.

00:13:29.809 --> 00:13:30.853
Hurry, follow me!

00:13:30.984 --> 00:13:32.376
[shrieks]
Who the hell are you?

00:13:32.507 --> 00:13:33.813
Station doctor
Harrison Horseberry.

00:13:33.943 --> 00:13:35.727
We must get these officers
to Sickbay.

00:13:35.815 --> 00:13:37.773
Posthaste.
Pip-pip, on your way.

00:13:37.904 --> 00:13:40.080
[growling]

00:13:40.167 --> 00:13:41.603
Um...

00:13:41.777 --> 00:13:42.734
Wh-What is happening
with your doctor?

00:13:42.865 --> 00:13:44.606
Oh, yeah, he gets that a lot.

00:13:44.693 --> 00:13:46.608
[whispers]:
He's British.

00:13:46.738 --> 00:13:48.523
Does he have one of those
Tarchannen parasites

00:13:48.653 --> 00:13:49.350
that mess with your DNA?

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:50.699
I used to have one.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:52.440
I got it from sharing
a toothbrush

00:13:52.527 --> 00:13:54.137
with one of my colleges.

00:13:54.268 --> 00:13:55.965
How did you know? I was told
it was hardly noticeable.

00:13:56.052 --> 00:13:57.575
Yeah, it was...
it was little noticeable.

00:13:57.749 --> 00:13:59.055
HORSEBERRY:
[gasps] Oh, my word.

00:13:59.142 --> 00:14:01.014
- This can't be right.
- W-What's wrong?

00:14:01.144 --> 00:14:03.625
Nothing. No pathogens
or biochemical phenomena

00:14:03.712 --> 00:14:05.322
and no Tarchannen parasites,

00:14:05.409 --> 00:14:06.846
which I always check for,
just for fun.

00:14:06.976 --> 00:14:09.936
Oh, my God. You're right.
It is a curse!

00:14:10.023 --> 00:14:11.720
All right, [bleep] this.
I'm calling for evac.

00:14:11.851 --> 00:14:12.764
Stop!
Give me that combadge.

00:14:12.895 --> 00:14:14.114
- You'll get it, too!
- Hey!

00:14:15.202 --> 00:14:17.030
[gasps] I knew
you were up to something.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.118
[grunting]

00:14:23.732 --> 00:14:24.864
[grunting]

00:14:27.214 --> 00:14:29.172
Holly [bleep].
How are you so good at fighting?

00:14:29.303 --> 00:14:32.306
I'm El-Aurian.
I think I know how to fight.

00:14:32.436 --> 00:14:34.003
Wait, like Guinan?

00:14:34.134 --> 00:14:35.744
What, so you're, like,
400 years old?

00:14:35.875 --> 00:14:38.094
No, I'm in my 30s.
But I pay attention.

00:14:38.225 --> 00:14:40.749
A young El-Aurian
is just a regular person!

00:14:40.836 --> 00:14:41.968
I'm trying to protect you.

00:14:42.142 --> 00:14:44.013
Sure doesn't feel like it.

00:14:44.187 --> 00:14:47.538
Have you noticed your crew
only starts acting weird

00:14:47.669 --> 00:14:49.714
after using their combadges?

00:14:49.801 --> 00:14:51.891
- So?
- So, what if that's why

00:14:51.978 --> 00:14:53.936
your crew's affected
and ours isn't?

00:14:54.023 --> 00:14:55.895
Everyone here's
acting weird as [bleep].

00:14:57.287 --> 00:15:00.638
They're goofy and excentric,
but not licking walls.

00:15:00.812 --> 00:15:01.988
- [grunts]
- We don't have combadges.

00:15:02.118 --> 00:15:04.991
We use old wall comms.
That has to be it.

00:15:05.121 --> 00:15:06.427
Boimler just contacted
his ensigns.

00:15:06.557 --> 00:15:08.646
[grunts]
And he's fine.

00:15:08.777 --> 00:15:10.953
- [growling]
- Oh, [bleep],

00:15:12.737 --> 00:15:14.739
Oh, my God, you were right.
It's the combadges.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:17.873
But that means the curse
is from the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos?&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:19.483 --> 00:15:21.007
Sorry, Boims.
[grunts]

00:15:22.356 --> 00:15:23.357
[panting]

00:15:23.487 --> 00:15:25.359
[whoops]

00:15:25.446 --> 00:15:28.144
[grunting]

00:15:28.275 --> 00:15:29.841
[groans]

00:15:29.929 --> 00:15:31.669
RANSOM:
Wow, that's a lot
of Acamarians.

00:15:31.843 --> 00:15:34.629
Careful, Cap.
These guys can get pretty rough.

00:15:34.759 --> 00:15:36.457
You lost, Starfleet?

00:15:36.587 --> 00:15:39.590
We don't get a lot
of your kind around here.

00:15:39.721 --> 00:15:41.766
Unless they're going to...

00:15:41.853 --> 00:15:44.073
the arcade.

00:15:44.204 --> 00:15:46.554
We are going to the arcade.

00:15:46.684 --> 00:15:48.512
Oh, awesome.
It's right over there.

00:15:48.686 --> 00:15:51.124
Here's some extra tokens.
On the house.

00:15:54.214 --> 00:15:55.519
[grunting]

00:15:55.606 --> 00:15:57.391
- BOTH: Gene?
- Oh!

00:15:57.521 --> 00:15:58.783
Howdy, friends.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:00.220
That is it.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.483
I don't know what
you've been up to, buddy,

00:16:02.613 --> 00:16:03.440
but it ends now.

00:16:03.571 --> 00:16:04.572
No more runarounds.

00:16:04.659 --> 00:16:06.617
Where's Lt. Jakobowski?

00:16:06.704 --> 00:16:08.097
Aw, calm down, lady.

00:16:08.228 --> 00:16:10.752
- That is Jakobowski.
- What?

00:16:10.882 --> 00:16:14.147
Chief Engineer Gene Jakobowski
at your service.

00:16:14.277 --> 00:16:16.758
You better have
a damn good explanation, Gene.

00:16:16.932 --> 00:16:20.153
I know, apologies,
apologies for the subterfuge.

00:16:20.327 --> 00:16:22.285
I've been asking Starfleet
to send someone

00:16:22.459 --> 00:16:25.158
to help with repairs
for months, see?

00:16:25.288 --> 00:16:27.290
I couldn't miss a chance
to get help fixing

00:16:27.464 --> 00:16:29.510
the alarms and oxygen pipe.

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:32.252
Starfleet lying to Starfleet?
That is messed-up, Gene.

00:16:32.382 --> 00:16:34.732
Well, if you help me
clear out the bats

00:16:34.906 --> 00:16:37.083
in subsection five,
I'll give you

00:16:37.213 --> 00:16:38.954
your navigation processor.

00:16:39.085 --> 00:16:40.695
No way are we helping you
with that.

00:16:40.825 --> 00:16:42.088
You go get it right now.

00:16:42.218 --> 00:16:43.089
Captain?

00:16:43.263 --> 00:16:45.134
No, I-I get it.

00:16:45.221 --> 00:16:46.918
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;
isn't the flashiest ship,

00:16:47.049 --> 00:16:49.573
so it's easy
for command to ignore.

00:16:49.704 --> 00:16:52.576
You know what, I haven't been
exactly fair to you today.

00:16:52.707 --> 00:16:55.057
Let's get those bats.

00:16:55.144 --> 00:16:57.059
[screaming, clamoring]

00:17:02.543 --> 00:17:04.197
[both exclaim]

00:17:05.459 --> 00:17:06.416
[gasps]

00:17:06.547 --> 00:17:08.027
[exclaiming]

00:17:08.114 --> 00:17:10.681
Oh, I can't believe
I messed this up.

00:17:10.812 --> 00:17:12.422
You didn't do anything.

00:17:12.553 --> 00:17:13.641
Getting kicked off my ship
and being transferred here--

00:17:13.728 --> 00:17:15.295
that was my rock bottom.

00:17:15.382 --> 00:17:17.558
Being back made me feel like
I was still that person.

00:17:17.688 --> 00:17:18.863
If I'd been on my game,

00:17:18.994 --> 00:17:20.213
I would have seen
what was happening.

00:17:20.387 --> 00:17:21.910
Hey, this isn't
rock bottom for anyone.

00:17:22.041 --> 00:17:23.738
Starbase 80's
for second chances.

00:17:23.912 --> 00:17:25.131
That's why I love it.

00:17:25.261 --> 00:17:28.482
[gasps] What the...
What is that?

00:17:28.569 --> 00:17:30.005
[shouts]

00:17:30.136 --> 00:17:32.399
I mean, when you
put it like that,

00:17:32.529 --> 00:17:34.270
I'm kind of into Starbase 80.

00:17:34.401 --> 00:17:36.272
We're not perfect,
but that's why it works.

00:17:36.359 --> 00:17:38.405
Damn.
Okay, so it's not a curse.

00:17:38.535 --> 00:17:40.711
Something is piggybacking
on our combadge signals.

00:17:40.842 --> 00:17:42.757
We have to find the source.

00:17:48.241 --> 00:17:50.765
[gasps] There's
a biological energy signature.

00:17:50.852 --> 00:17:52.767
Then your comm logs can tell us
how this started.

00:17:52.854 --> 00:17:54.334
Yeah, they're back on the ship,
which will be full

00:17:54.421 --> 00:17:56.336
of cursed crew. How are
we gonna get through that?

00:17:56.423 --> 00:17:59.730
With the help of two
of my biggest weirdos.

00:17:59.904 --> 00:18:02.777
♪

00:18:06.563 --> 00:18:08.304
We need to get to the bridge.
Let's use caution...

00:18:08.478 --> 00:18:10.437
&lt;i&gt;- COMPUTER: Self-destruct
sequence activated.&lt;/i&gt;
- What?!

00:18:10.611 --> 00:18:12.569
&lt;i&gt;Self-destruct sequence aborted.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:12.656 --> 00:18:13.918
Oh, thank God.

00:18:14.049 --> 00:18:15.311
&lt;i&gt;Self-destruct sequence
activated.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:15.442 --> 00:18:17.531
What the hell is happening
on this ship?

00:18:17.618 --> 00:18:19.750
Forget caution!
New plan: reckless abandon!

00:18:19.837 --> 00:18:23.406
&lt;i&gt;Self-self-self-self-
self-self-destruct...&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:23.537 --> 00:18:25.539
&lt;i&gt;self-destruct-
self-destruct sequence...&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:25.669 --> 00:18:27.802
[hisses]

00:18:27.932 --> 00:18:29.630
Pardon me!

00:18:31.458 --> 00:18:33.329
[moaning]

00:18:33.416 --> 00:18:34.765
Livik.

00:18:34.896 --> 00:18:36.419
[grunts]

00:18:37.507 --> 00:18:40.380
- Nice.
- Happens all the time
on our base.

00:18:40.467 --> 00:18:41.511
Whoa!

00:18:41.642 --> 00:18:43.557
My stars!

00:18:43.644 --> 00:18:44.993
There's no way through.
We have to go back.

00:18:45.167 --> 00:18:47.735
Looks like
this is a job for Chad.

00:18:47.865 --> 00:18:50.564
Corn dogs, ho!

00:18:50.694 --> 00:18:53.219
Chad, no!

00:18:55.743 --> 00:18:56.570
Keep going.

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:57.788
Chad'll be okay.

00:18:57.919 --> 00:19:00.443
[moans, grunting]

00:19:00.617 --> 00:19:02.358
Chad!

00:19:03.359 --> 00:19:04.447
&lt;i&gt;Self-destruct-
self-destruct se...&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:04.621 --> 00:19:05.883
&lt;i&gt;self-destruct sequence...&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:06.014 --> 00:19:07.798
&lt;i&gt;self-destruct sequence ac...&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:07.929 --> 00:19:10.410
&lt;i&gt;Self-destruct sequence aborted.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:10.497 --> 00:19:12.194
- [exhales]
- KASSIA: I isolated

00:19:12.325 --> 00:19:13.369
the source
of the combadge signal.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.631
- Where is this?
- What?

00:19:14.762 --> 00:19:17.199
No way.

00:19:19.941 --> 00:19:22.291
You have whales?!

00:19:22.378 --> 00:19:23.466
They do stellar navigation
and they also

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.729
- throw really crazy parties.
- Shh!

00:19:27.427 --> 00:19:29.255
Get down!

00:19:36.305 --> 00:19:37.828
- What's he doing?
- I don't know. That's new.

00:19:37.959 --> 00:19:39.265
Okay, good news.

00:19:39.395 --> 00:19:40.962
Pretty sure
it's not Tarchannen parasites.

00:19:41.136 --> 00:19:42.224
Has he been off the ship lately?

00:19:42.355 --> 00:19:44.835
He was on an away mission
on Piskes Nine.

00:19:44.966 --> 00:19:47.055
HORSEBERRY:
I'm reading an anaphasic
conscious controlling his body.

00:19:47.186 --> 00:19:49.188
It appears
to have spread throughout

00:19:49.318 --> 00:19:51.494
the entire &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; crew,
but its central mind is here.

00:19:51.581 --> 00:19:53.975
So, everyone is licking
and touching the walls

00:19:54.105 --> 00:19:55.585
because they're
like his fingertips,

00:19:55.716 --> 00:19:58.109
- reaching out in the dark.
- Finger and tongue tips, yeah.

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.937
Can you reverse the effects,
Doctor?

00:20:00.068 --> 00:20:01.939
Perhaps, if I could
just get close enough.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:04.594
Not an option.
We can't lose anyone else.

00:20:04.725 --> 00:20:07.467
[groans] I spent all day
thinking you guys were idiots.

00:20:07.597 --> 00:20:10.078
Now it's my turn to be
the biggest idiot of all.

00:20:10.209 --> 00:20:13.647
Come and get me,
you crazy energy ghost!

00:20:14.952 --> 00:20:16.780
[shouts, whimpers]

00:20:16.911 --> 00:20:18.391
[shouts, grunts]

00:20:18.521 --> 00:20:21.481
Hurry, I feel myself
getting moronic. [moans]

00:20:21.568 --> 00:20:23.047
Mariner!

00:20:23.134 --> 00:20:24.962
[gasps]
What are you doing?

00:20:25.093 --> 00:20:26.921
Giving you a second chance.

00:20:27.704 --> 00:20:28.879
[both grunt]

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:29.880
[shouts]

00:20:30.011 --> 00:20:31.926
[both moaning]

00:20:32.883 --> 00:20:34.581
[whimpering]

00:20:34.755 --> 00:20:36.452
Stop! Doctor's orders!

00:20:36.539 --> 00:20:37.758
[whimpers]

00:20:37.888 --> 00:20:39.542
I've studied
the most advanced medicines

00:20:39.673 --> 00:20:42.893
in the quadrant, but some
problems need an old-fashioned

00:20:43.024 --> 00:20:45.200
bonking!

00:20:45.331 --> 00:20:46.549
[retches]

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:48.812
[grunting]

00:20:48.899 --> 00:20:50.553
[both grunting]

00:20:50.727 --> 00:20:51.859
What? Where am I?

00:20:51.989 --> 00:20:54.078
Oh, Doc, how'd you do it?

00:20:54.209 --> 00:20:55.906
[clears throat] Um, uh,

00:20:56.037 --> 00:20:58.561
complicated doctor stuff.

00:20:58.735 --> 00:21:00.476
Oh, boy.

00:21:00.607 --> 00:21:02.173
[gasps]

00:21:02.304 --> 00:21:03.349
[all gasp]

00:21:03.523 --> 00:21:04.872
[moans]
Wha...

00:21:04.959 --> 00:21:06.656
What happened?
Eh...

00:21:08.745 --> 00:21:11.400
Chad lives to dog another day.

00:21:14.795 --> 00:21:16.927
&lt;i&gt;KASSIA:
Base commander's log,
supplemental.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:17.058 --> 00:21:19.060
&lt;i&gt;With the anaphasic
entity contained,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.844
&lt;i&gt;Dr. Horseberry
was able to set up&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:21.018 --> 00:21:22.759
&lt;i&gt;a stable vessel
for it to inhabit.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:25.327
CLEM:
My designation is Clem.

00:21:25.414 --> 00:21:27.068
I am sorry for the trouble
I've caused.

00:21:27.155 --> 00:21:29.113
Thank you for not destroying me.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:30.593
No problem, Clem.

00:21:30.724 --> 00:21:32.116
Welcome to Starbase 80.

00:21:32.247 --> 00:21:33.640
I can't believe
you're letting it stay here.

00:21:33.814 --> 00:21:35.946
We'll be fine as long as Clem

00:21:36.033 --> 00:21:37.208
doesn't try to inhabit anyone.

00:21:37.383 --> 00:21:38.862
CLEM:
I will not.

00:21:38.993 --> 00:21:40.864
Why did you possess anyone
in the first place?

00:21:40.995 --> 00:21:43.389
CLEM:
To prove to my superiors
that I'm capable

00:21:43.519 --> 00:21:46.000
of communicating
with corporeal species.

00:21:46.087 --> 00:21:48.829
Hold up, so you're, like,
a junior anaphasic alien?

00:21:48.959 --> 00:21:51.919
CLEM:
Correct, but the amount
of mind merges overwhelmed me.

00:21:52.049 --> 00:21:53.399
I took over too many hosts.

00:21:53.573 --> 00:21:55.314
Spread myself too thin.

00:21:55.488 --> 00:21:58.360
But now we're communicating,
so it's a win for everyone.

00:21:58.447 --> 00:21:59.927
CLEM:
I hope my bosses
see it that way.

00:22:00.014 --> 00:22:02.059
They can be real dicks.

00:22:02.233 --> 00:22:04.801
Well, Mariner,
I guess that solves the curse

00:22:04.932 --> 00:22:06.977
and your navigational problems.

00:22:07.064 --> 00:22:09.937
It's been a pleasure
having you on Starbase 80.

00:22:10.067 --> 00:22:12.156
Oh, we aren't done yet.

00:22:12.287 --> 00:22:14.376
[chuckles]
We aren't?

00:22:17.901 --> 00:22:19.076
[grunts]

00:22:19.207 --> 00:22:21.035
Okey-dokey, that should do it.

00:22:21.209 --> 00:22:23.080
Everyone hold on to something.

00:22:23.211 --> 00:22:25.431
[rumbling, whirring]

00:22:28.608 --> 00:22:30.740
Oh, thank you for fixing
the grav-plating.

00:22:30.871 --> 00:22:33.439
It's gonna feel real good not
to fall to the ceiling in here.

00:22:33.569 --> 00:22:35.397
Yeah, maybe fixing up
all your little problems

00:22:35.484 --> 00:22:37.443
will help make up
for me being such a jerk.

00:22:37.573 --> 00:22:39.662
You were just watching out
for your friends.

00:22:39.793 --> 00:22:41.621
And, hopefully, now you see

00:22:41.751 --> 00:22:43.927
we're just a bunch
of scrappy underdogs.

00:22:44.058 --> 00:22:45.407
Arf, arf!
[chuckles]

00:22:45.538 --> 00:22:47.409
Now, that I can understand.
[gasps]

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:48.976
Wait, has anyone
seen the captain?

00:22:49.106 --> 00:22:50.499
Uh, someone told her
we don't need

00:22:50.630 --> 00:22:52.414
the repair materials
anymore, right?

00:22:52.545 --> 00:22:54.721
[shouts, grunts]

00:22:54.851 --> 00:22:56.418
You don't have anything more
to prove, Captain.

00:22:56.505 --> 00:22:58.115
- Let's get out of here.
- No!

00:22:58.246 --> 00:22:59.856
The alternate Freeman
must have failed at this

00:22:59.987 --> 00:23:02.511
and I won't!
There's still the big one.

00:23:02.642 --> 00:23:04.644
[growling]

00:23:04.731 --> 00:23:06.385
But it won't even
fit in the cage!

00:23:06.515 --> 00:23:08.474
Yeah, not with that attitude,
it won't.

00:23:08.561 --> 00:23:10.301
How about I just
forge the signature?

00:23:10.476 --> 00:23:11.955
[shouting]

00:23:12.129 --> 00:23:13.392
&lt;i&gt;No giant [bleep] bat&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:13.522 --> 00:23:15.785
&lt;i&gt;is keeping me
on this goddamn station!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:15.916 --> 00:23:17.483
&lt;i&gt;- [bat screeches]
- [Freeman grunts]&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:17.613 --> 00:23:19.180
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM:
Look out for the claws, Captain!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:21.312
&lt;i&gt;- [Freeman screams]
- RANSOM: The claws!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:25.752 --> 00:23:28.929
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:24:16.019 --> 00:24:17.412
[man imitates weapons firing]

00:24:19.414 --> 00:24:21.372
Chirp.
